# mpd.env — per-project configuration for a cftunnel project.
#
# A cftunnel project runs one Cloudflare tunnel connector
# (`cloudflared`) authenticated with a CF tunnel token. The tunnel
# itself and its public hostname routes are configured on the
# Cloudflare side; one cftunnel project can fulfill many routes
# pointing at many internal mpd projects.
#
# Required user setup (one-time, lives in ~/.mpd/mpd-user.env):
#   MPD_UTIL_CFTUNNEL_DOMAIN=.your-public-domain.org
# This is the domain pattern target projects use to compute their
# expected public hostname for the wwwroot rewrite.
#
# Per-target opt-in (on each moodle/etc. project to be exposed):
#   mpd configure <target> MPD_PHP_MOODLE_CFTUNNEL=1
# Without that, Caddy frontdoor will not serve the tunnel hostname
# for the target — even if the CF dashboard route exists, the request
# falls through to Caddy's default. This is the per-project access
# control: only projects that have explicitly opted in are reachable
# via the tunnel.
#
# Cloudflare-side setup (per route, in CF dashboard):
#   1. Create a Cloudflare Tunnel; copy the token below.
#   2. Public Hostnames: for each moodle (or other) project to
#      expose, add a route:
#        - Subdomain: <project>
#        - Domain: <your-public-domain>
#        - Service Type: HTTPS
#        - Service URL: <project>.mpd.test
#   3. Strongly recommended: gate each route with Cloudflare Access
#      so the URL is not reachable by the open internet.

# Cloudflare Tunnel token. Required.
MPD_CFTUNNEL_TOKEN=""

# This project type doesn't use a database.
MPD_DB=""
